be. Nothing here is derived from a licence to redistribute the game.

**What the page fetches, and on whose say-so.** The pages read a copy of the
game that you supply — dropped on the page, picked from disk, served beside
it, or named with `?src=`. Where you supply none, the page offers to fetch an
installer that the Internet Archive already hosts publicly, and says so, with
its size, on a screen you have to click through before anything is downloaded.
That fetch goes from your browser to archive.org; the bytes are not served
from this repository, are not mirrored by it, and no copy of them is kept here.
Use a copy you are entitled to use.

**Why it is the whole installer and never one file out of it.** The licence
Ambrosia shipped with the game (`Cythera License.text`, in the installed
folder's `Documentation ƒ`) says: "Non-profit distribution of the software is
acceptable without prior written notice, providing that the software is not
modified in any way, and the complete works of the software are included in
the distribution package." The page reads one file, `Cythera Data`, and could
fetch that alone at a fifth of the size; it fetches the complete, unmodified
installer instead, and says so on the same screen, so that what passes between
archive.org and your browser is the whole work and not a piece of it. That is
a condition of Ambrosia's terms as written, not a preference about file
formats.

**Nothing of the game's is in `res/`.** Until 17 September 2026 the directory
held three files taken out of the game: a plank tile, a capture of the
dialogue-box frame, and the Argos A Nouveau typeface. The page had stopped
using each of them earlier in the month, drawing the tile and the frame out of
the open file's own resources and setting itself in Chicago Kare until a file
is open, and the maintainer removed them that day. They remain in this
repository's history and are Ambrosia's or their respective authors', not ours.

**`res/ChicagoKare-Regular.woff2`** is **Chicago Kare** by **Duane King**
(<https://github.com/kingduane/Chicago-Kare>), a reproduction of the bitmap
Chicago typeface **Susan Kare** drew for Apple in 1984, licensed **MIT**. The
licence text is beside it as `res/ChicagoKare-LICENSE.txt` and governs it. It
is the face this page is set in before any game file is open, and it is not
Ambrosia's.

**`res/CarthageSans-Regular.woff2`** is **Carthage Sans** by **Brian Connors**
(csyde, <https://fontstruct.com/fontstructions/show/1172663>), a reimagining of
Apple's **Espy Sans** bitmap font, which is the face Cythera's application names
for its Text and Lang0 styles. The package is dual licensed **SIL Open Font
License 1.1** and **CC-BY-SA 4.0**, at the user's choice, and its `license.txt`
is beside it as `res/CarthageSans-LICENSE.txt`. The page uses it for the marks
Chicago Kare does not carry. Two things to know about the file, neither of them
a change we made to it: the regular weight's embedded licence field reads
"FontStruct Non-Commercial License", where the package's own `license.txt`, the
author's readme and every other weight in the family say OFL and CC-BY-SA -- the
string is left as he shipped it; and converting a TrueType to woff2 is a format
change, which the OFL counts as a modification, so the name here is the family's
own only because the design is untouched.

**`res/Geneva9-1-Regular.woff2`** is **Geneva 9.1** by **Kelsey Higham**
(<https://fontstruct.com/fontstructions/show/1304775>), a pixel-exact clone of
the 9-point **Geneva** bitmap Susan Kare drew for Apple in 1984, licensed under
the **SIL Open Font License 1.1**. The licence and the readme FontStruct
requires to travel with it are beside it as `res/Geneva9-1-LICENSE.txt` and
`res/Geneva9-1-README.txt`. It is the page's text face, because Geneva 9 and 10
is what Cythera's own data file names for its Labels, Stats and Text styles.
Geneva itself is Apple's; this is a clone of the bitmap, and Apple's own
TrueType Geneva is not here.

**`delvmod/`** is a submodule, so this repository stores only a pointer to it.
It is an independent work by **Bryce Schroeder**
(<https://github.com/BryceSchroeder/delvmod>), licensed **GPLv3**, and is used
here for data inspection and as a correctness oracle. Its licence governs it.
The submodule points at a fork of it, which carries Python 3 fixes and says so
in its README; the work is his.
